(5164181, 749396, 76335, '<td valign="top">Good one, Joe, and a respectable finish. You got a nine from me. You nailed the challenge criteria. Good use of compositional technique here also...</td>', 'Good one, Joe, and a respectable finish. You got a nine from me. You nailed the challenge criteria. Good use of compositional technique here also...', '2009-01-01 22:09:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5164492, 749396, 16241, '<td valign="top">you beat me, bitch.</td>', 'you beat me, bitch.', '2009-01-02 02:12:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(5165235, 748868, 811, '<td valign="top">CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUE<br/>by karmat<br/> <br/>First off, I was one of your 3 nines, so I obviously like it.  :)<br/> <br/>Compositionally, I really like how the main subject is "anchored" in the lower left of the picture, and is balanced by the shadow on the right.  I think the balance would have been stronger if the shadow had been a bit further to the right, though.  I also think the square (or nearly square -- I didn''t measure) works well.<br/> <br/>Technically, the exposure is good as well as lighting, color, focus, etc.  The contrast level that several mentioned looks good to me, unless they are referring to the shadow -- it would have been nice if that was darker, somehow.<br/> <br/>Overall, it is a technically strong shot, and it meets the challenge.  When I first looked at it, I could tell the shadow was Santa.  But, looking at it longer, I can see how some may not have seen that, and as a result, the shot may not have been as obvious.  The expression is also great!<br/> <br/>Good work, and best to you in future challenges.<br/> <br/>Karma</td>', 'CRITIQUE CLUB CRITIQUEby karmat First off, I was one of your 3 nines, so I obviously like it.  :) Compositionally, I really like how the main subject is "anchored" in the lower left of the picture, and is balanced by the shadow on the right.  I think the balance would have been stronger if the shadow had been a bit further to the right, though.  I also think the square (or nearly square -- I didn''t measure) works well. Technically, the exposure is good as well as lighting, color, focus, etc.  The contrast level that several mentioned looks good to me, unless they are referring to the shadow -- it would have been nice if that was darker, somehow. Overall, it is a technically strong shot, and it meets the challenge.  When I first looked at it, I could tell the shadow was Santa.  But, looking at it longer, I can see how some may not have seen that, and as a result, the shot may not have been as obvious.  The expression is also great! Good work, and best to you in future challenges. Karma', '2009-01-02 13:39:48.000000', NULL, 0),
